issue_context.body:
Consider

```C#
using System;
using System.Formats.Asn1;

AsnWriter writer = new(AsnEncodingRules.DER);
writer.WriteNamedBitList<Foo>(Foo.Eight);
byte[] encoded = writer.Encode();

[Flags]
enum Foo : sbyte
{
    None = 0b00000000,
    One = 0b00000001,
    Two = 0b00000010,
    Three = 0b00000100,
    Four = 0b00001000,
    Five = 0b00010000,
    Six = 0b00100000,
    Seven = 0b01000000,
    Eight = unchecked((sbyte)0b10000000),
}
```

This will encode as `03090001FFFFFFFFFFFFFF`.

I am not exactly sure what the expected behavior is, perhaps encode it as if it were unsigned like `03020001`, or perhaps encoding negative enum values for signed enum types should be prohibited.
